cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its predictions, please cite it as below.
title: "NanoMatAI: band gaps of 2D semiconductors from crystal structure, with a calibrated trust verdict"
abstract: >-
  A CGCNN ensemble that predicts the band gap of a two-dimensional monolayer from
  its crystal structure on CPU, together with a calibrated uncertainty interval and
  an explicit verdict on whether the prediction is usable. Trained on 13 349 stable
  2D semiconductors from Alexandria and evaluated on a composition-disjoint split
  (MAE 0.246 eV). The graph reads bond angles as well as bond lengths, which is what
  lets it separate polymorphs of one composition. Three independent out-of-domain
  checks decide the verdict: a metal/semiconductor gate, the spread between ensemble
  members, and the distance to the training set in the model's own latent space.
  Linear heads on that same latent space add a quasiparticle gap, an exciton binding
  energy and an absorption onset, and a second ensemble adds the work function, so
  the band edges a contact metal is chosen on follow from the pair. Predictions for
  28 372 public 2D structures are published as a browsable table.
type: software
authors:
